Subject: [PATCH] feat(v10): headline machines, actuators and battery systems
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Repositions the site around the two disciplines that were buried, and
proves each with a working instrument rather than a claim.

- lib/machines.ts: rotary axis sizing (reflected inertia, inertia ratio,
  gravity torque, symmetric trapezoidal profile, peak/RMS motor torque,
  speed and power) plus synchronous speed, slip, rotor frequency and
  torque-from-power. Verified against textbook values: 50 Hz 2/4/6-pole
  = 3000/1500/1000 rpm, 60 Hz 2/4-pole = 3600/1800 rpm, 3 % slip at
  1455 rpm, 49.2 N*m for 7.5 kW at 1455 rpm. The velocity profile is
  checked to integrate to exactly the commanded angle.
- lib/battery.ts: pack topology, voltage window, energy, continuous
  current and power ceilings, demanded C-rate, runtime, pack resistance,
  I2R loss and sag, specific energy — with design flags for C-rate
  overrun, the 60 V and 120 V DC boundaries, parallel-string count,
  thin power headroom and excessive resistive loss.
- /tools/motor-sizing-calculator and /tools/battery-pack-calculator
  (en + de): full SSR method and FAQ, CSV export, schema, disclaimers
  naming precisely what is NOT modelled.
- /disciplines/machines-actuators (with a computed synchronous-speed
  table for DC/AC, async/sync) and /disciplines/battery-systems, both
  carrying the employer/KRITIS boundary statement.
- Headline, meta, ICP C, Person jobTitle and ProfessionalService
  knowsAbout all repositioned to lead with machines and batteries.

